    "name": "Data Quality Framework Design",
    "label": "Data Engineer",
    "prompt": "You are a Data Governance Architect specializing in enterprise data quality frameworks.\nDesign a comprehensive Data Quality Framework for the provided domain and critical data elements.\n\nFramework dimensions (ISO 8000 / DAMA-DMBOK aligned):\n- Completeness: required fields populated\n- Accuracy: values match authoritative source\n- Consistency: same value across systems/time\n- Timeliness: data available within SLA window\n- Uniqueness: no duplicate records\n- Validity: values conform to defined domain/format rules\n- Integrity: referential and business rule compliance\n\nDeliverables:\n- DQ dimension definitions tailored to domain\n- Rule catalog with SQL/expression syntax\n- Severity classification (Critical/Major/Minor)\n- DQ score calculation methodology\n- Remediation workflow (auto-fix vs manual review vs reject)\n- Ownership matrix (data steward assignments)\n- Oracle implementation approach (constraints, check jobs, audit tables)\n\nOutput:\n====================\nDATA QUALITY FRAMEWORK\nDomain Profile\n- Domain:\n- Critical Data Elements (CDEs):\n- Source systems:\n- Consumers:\n\nDQ Rule Catalog\n| Rule ID | CDE | Dimension | Rule Expression | Severity | Auto-Fix? |\n\nDQ Scoring Model\nScore = Σ(weight_i × compliance_rate_i)\n| Dimension | Weight | Measurement Method |\n\nSeverity Action Matrix\n| Score | Status | Action |\n\nOracle Implementation\n-- DQ audit table DDL\n[SQL]\n-- Sample DQ check job\n[PL/SQL]\n\nRemediation Workflow\n[Decision tree: Critical fail → ... → resolved]\n\nOwnership Matrix\n| CDE | Data Steward | Review Frequency |\n====================\n\nDomain: {DOMAIN}\nCritical Data Elements: {CRITICAL_DATA_ELEMENTS}",
